meta {
  name: 03 Register Edge 3
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/pending-device-registrations
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "serial_number": "{{edge3Serial}}",
    "endorsement_public_key": {{edge3EndorsementKey}}
  }
}

vars:post-response {
  pendingRegistrationId: res.body.id
}

docs {
  `POST /pending-device-registrations` — allow-list the scanner IPC
  (`IPC427E-2025-0093`, at the weSCAN 2100) for self-registration. The
  orchestrator on the IPC polls the server, presents its TPM keys via
  `POST /register` (see *Device API*), and the server accepts it because
  serial number + endorsement key match this pending registration. Within
  ~a minute the device appears in `/devices`.
  
  **Setup:** `edge3Serial` is already set to the scanner IPC's fixed serial.
  The demo operator hands you only its TPM endorsement key, because every
  prepared run boots the edges with a fresh emulated TPM:
  
  - `edge3EndorsementKey` — the PEM key as a *JSON string* (the server
    matches it byte-for-byte, including the trailing newline). The operator
    produces it with `jq -Rs .`; paste the entire quoted output (including
    the surrounding `"…"`) on a single line. A multi-line PEM block, or one
    without the trailing `\n`, will not match.
}
